    {
      "id": "claim_5d3735212f39419a90cc15dc439f0c39",
      "statement": "Lifecycle hooks (before_model, after_model) support conditional control flow via jump_to field in returned state dictionaries, with valid destinations being 'model' (retry model invocation), 'tools' (execute tool node), and 'end' (exit agent loop). Jumping capability must be declared upfront via @hook_config decorator or can_jump_to parameter on lifecycle hook decorators; interception hooks cannot use jump_to directly and unsupported Command directives (goto, resume, graph) raise NotImplementedError.",
      "evidence": [
